ability. Thus, other low-cost and simple evaluations could be used, especially\nin the ﬁeld. From these tests, incremental ﬁeld-testing for identiﬁcation of maximum aerobic speed\n(MAS) could be considered the most practical, as MAS integrates both VO2max and RE into a single\nparameter and was used", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["injury_safety", "training_protocol"], "text": "the ﬁeld was also suggested to\nbe valid in identifying the anaerobic threshold along with the MAS [62]. Of note, ﬁeld running testing\ncould be more diﬃcult to apply due to the constraints associated with ﬁeld and weather conditions.\nHowever, ﬁeld te", "language": "en", "quality_tier": "expert_review_narrative", "domain_pack": "injury_prevention_and_rehab", "review_status": "auto_classified", "needs_review": false, "prescription_permission": "explanation_only", "evidence_weight": "moderate", "auto_classification_basis": "quality_tier", "can_write_core": false}
