tandard deviation) and\nstrain (i.e., weekly sRPE × monotony) could be very helpful to avoid overreaching and overtraining,\nrequiring only the recording of this simple information on a daily basis [68].\nFinally, over the last decade, a number of studies pointed out the validity and practicality ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["injury_safety", "training_protocol"], "text": "load indices such as monotony (i.e., mean weekly sRPE/standard deviation) and\nstrain (i.e., weekly sRPE × monotony) could be very helpful to avoid overreaching and overtraining,\nrequiring only the recording of this simple information on a daily basis", "language": "en", "quality_tier": "expert_review_narrative", "domain_pack": "injury_prevention_and_rehab", "review_status": "auto_classified", "needs_review": false, "prescription_permission": "explanation_only", "evidence_weight": "moderate", "auto_classification_basis": "quality_tier", "can_write_core": false}
