ibility but might negatively impact endurance running economy [20]; therefore, stretching could be\nperformed to allow normal range of mobility during running.\nThe available evidence is insuﬃcient to determine whether total energy intake per day or\nmacronutrient and micronutrient proportions in the", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["injury_safety", "training_protocol"], "text": "ihood of injury [164,165]. Recent evidence suggested that optimal shoe cushioning\nproperties might diﬀer depending on the athlete’s body mass, because greater shoe cushioning might\nonly beneﬁt lighter runners [166].\nThe use of stretching exercises ha", "language": "en", "quality_tier": "expert_review_narrative", "domain_pack": "injury_prevention_and_rehab", "review_status": "auto_classified", "needs_review": false, "prescription_permission": "explanation_only", "evidence_weight": "moderate", "auto_classification_basis": "quality_tier", "can_write_core": false}
