oads of greater than 70% of maximum voluntary contraction (MVC) [29,32] or strains of\n4.5–6.5% [42–44] may deliver the appropriate loading‐induced tendon stimulus to initiate\nmechanotransduction pathways; however, the relationship of tendon force and resulting\nstrain can vary substantially between individuals [96,97]. Additionally, strain calcul", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["injury_safety"], "text": "3. Tendon Tissue Remodeling\nDespite the complex loading mechanics of the triceps surae MTU, not all loading is\ndetrimental to tendon health. While extrinsic factors contributing to tendon damage ap‐\npear to be primarily attributable to submaximal cyc", "language": "en", "quality_tier": "peer_reviewed_study", "domain_pack": "injury_prevention_and_rehab", "review_status": "auto_classified", "needs_review": false, "prescription_permission": "explanation_only", "evidence_weight": "moderate", "auto_classification_basis": "quality_tier", "can_write_core": false}
