\nother techniques for dissociation as high/low tempo music\nor if the external stimulus is among the subject's affective\npreferences for music or videos (Ballmann, 2021; Dyrlund\n& Wininger, 2008). Second, the sample size was based on\na convenient sample of well-­trained individuals and not\non an a priori statistical power calcula", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["injury_safety"], "text": "contently adjust-\ning speed and effort according to the route's topography,\nthe weather conditions, and the state of fatigue. Fourth,\nthe use and effect of self-­talk vary across cultural groups\nand the language spoken (Raalte & Vincent, 2017). Fina", "language": "en", "quality_tier": "randomized_controlled_trial", "domain_pack": "injury_prevention_and_rehab", "review_status": "auto_classified", "needs_review": false, "prescription_permission": "can_write_core", "evidence_weight": "strong", "auto_classification_basis": "quality_tier", "can_write_core": true}
