volume enables a greater skin and\nmuscle blood ﬂow and increases the\nsweating response (Figure 3). In mild\nheat stress, this means that perfor-\nmance can be likely maintained as\ncompared to cooler conditions with\nmore severe heat stress, heat acclima-\ntion mitigates but does not abolish\nheat-associated performance decre-\nThe profound me", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["injury_safety", "training_protocol"], "text": "d competition.\nFigure 3. Summary of the physiological underpinnings of heat-related decrements in\nrunning performance, and the mechanisms through which heat acclima-\ntion can reduce thermoregulatory and cardiovascular strain to improve\nhot-weather ru", "language": "en", "quality_tier": "peer_reviewed_study", "domain_pack": "injury_prevention_and_rehab", "review_status": "auto_classified", "needs_review": false, "prescription_permission": "explanation_only", "evidence_weight": "moderate", "auto_classification_basis": "quality_tier", "can_write_core": false}
