g and translate key ﬁnd-\nings from research into useable\nevidence-based recommendations for\npacing strategy preparation and\nadherence during competition.\nacing is the purposeful distribu-\ntion of speed, power, or energy\nprocess behind pacing (i.e., strategy)\nis recognized as an important element\nin endurance performance optimiza-\ntion. The challenge posed to runners\nis to avoid prem", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["injury_safety", "training_protocol"], "text": "gy)\nis recognized as an important element\nin endurance performance optimiza-\ntion. The challenge posed to runners\nis to avoid premature energy depletion\nresulting in fatigue or ﬁnishing a race\nwith excess energy resources. How run-\nners regulate exer", "language": "en", "quality_tier": "peer_reviewed_study", "domain_pack": "injury_prevention_and_rehab", "review_status": "auto_classified", "needs_review": false, "prescription_permission": "explanation_only", "evidence_weight": "moderate", "auto_classification_basis": "quality_tier", "can_write_core": false}
