anned recovery. Consider the possibilities in skill instruction, acquisition and the\nproposed goals throughout the phases as principal drivers of the training process will permit an optimal and\nflexible determination of the most appropriate training methods and ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["injury_safety", "training_protocol"], "text": "ts coming from physiological and biomechanical\nresearches as well as their experience and particular opinion.\n1. BAKER D. Applying in-Season Periodization of Strength and power Training to football. Strength\n2. BOMPA TO, HAFF GG. Periodization, Theor", "language": "en", "quality_tier": "peer_reviewed_study", "domain_pack": "injury_prevention_and_rehab", "review_status": "auto_classified", "needs_review": false, "prescription_permission": "explanation_only", "evidence_weight": "moderate", "auto_classification_basis": "quality_tier", "can_write_core": false}
