pplements typically as guarana,\nbissey nut, or kola. Caffeine can also be found in coffee,\ntea, soft drinks, energy drinks, and chocolate. Caffeine has\nalso been shown to be an effective ergogenic aid for aer-\nobic and anaerobic exercise with a documented ability to\nincrease energy expenditure and prom", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["injury_safety", "training_protocol"], "text": "to 4 min; im-\nprovements in neuromuscular fatigue, particularly in older\nsubjects, and lastly; potential benefits in tactical personnel\n[12]. Other studies have shown that ß-alanine supplemen-\ntation can increase the number of repetitions one can do", "language": "en", "quality_tier": "peer_reviewed_study", "domain_pack": "injury_prevention_and_rehab", "review_status": "auto_classified", "needs_review": false, "prescription_permission": "explanation_only", "evidence_weight": "moderate", "auto_classification_basis": "quality_tier", "can_write_core": false}
