 may im-\nprove VO2max and endurance capacity. A meta-analysis\nwas completed by Pelletier and researchers [617] to\nsummarize the potential impact of quercetin supplemen-\ntation on endurance performance. This analysis involved\nseven published studies representing 288 research partici", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["injury_safety"], "text": "ntly\nincreased strength, and decreased soreness and markers of\nmuscle damage [633]. Finally, studies have also supported\nthe ability of taurine to function in an anti-oxidative role,\nwhich may promote an improved cellular environment to\ntolerate exer", "language": "en", "quality_tier": "consensus_or_position_statement", "domain_pack": "injury_prevention_and_rehab", "review_status": "auto_classified", "needs_review": false, "prescription_permission": "can_write_core", "evidence_weight": "strong", "auto_classification_basis": "quality_tier", "can_write_core": true}
