ury free, to achieve a\nphysique that is suited to their event, and to perform at their best\non the day(s) of peak competitions.\nThe IAAF has long recognized the role of diet and nutrition\nstrategies in helping the athlete to achieve these goals. In 1995, it\nhosted the ﬁrst meeting on nut", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["injury_safety", "training_protocol"], "text": "The sport of athletics (track and ﬁeld) encompasses a wide\nrange of events involving running, walking, jumping, and\nthrowing, in which success is underpinned by a diversity of\nphysiological, psychological, and biomechanical attributes. Its\ngoverning", "language": "en", "quality_tier": "consensus_or_position_statement", "domain_pack": "injury_prevention_and_rehab", "review_status": "auto_classified", "needs_review": false, "prescription_permission": "can_write_core", "evidence_weight": "strong", "auto_classification_basis": "quality_tier", "can_write_core": true}
