ance in comparison with other training/\nTheme 11. Special Needs for Travel (Halson et al.,\nDomestic and international travel represents a regular challenge to\nhigh-performance Athletes, particularly when associated with the\npressure of competition or the need to support specialized train", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["injury_safety", "training_protocol"], "text": "high-performance Athletes, particularly when associated with the\npressure of competition or the need to support specialized training\n(e.g., altitude or heat adaptation). Jetlag is a challenge for trans-\nmeridian travelers while fatigue and alteratio", "language": "en", "quality_tier": "consensus_or_position_statement", "domain_pack": "injury_prevention_and_rehab", "review_status": "auto_classified", "needs_review": false, "prescription_permission": "can_write_core", "evidence_weight": "strong", "auto_classification_basis": "quality_tier", "can_write_core": true}
