 Availability in Females Questionnaire\n(LEAF-Q), which has been validated in female athletes\nto classify energy availability [111]. Two risk-assessment\ntools have been introduced by the Triad Coalition and the\nInternational Olympic Committee (IOC) [17, 112, 113]\nto aid the clinical decision-making process, ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["injury_safety", "medical_safety"], "text": "ed\nrisk for BSI compared with athletes classified in the low-\nrisk category [114]. The IOC REDs clinical assessment\ntool classifies athletes into low-, moderate- and high-risk\ncategories depending on subjective and objective exami-\nnation, particular", "language": "en", "quality_tier": "clinical_practice_guideline", "domain_pack": "injury_prevention_and_rehab", "review_status": "auto_classified", "needs_review": false, "prescription_permission": "can_write_core", "evidence_weight": "strong", "auto_classification_basis": "quality_tier", "can_write_core": true}
