ould participate in a wide range of\nsports and physical activities, includ-\nORGANIZATION OF THE TRAINING\nBefore specialization in a sport of\na young athlete’s choice, physical train-\ning should be semistructured and not\nemphasize peaking for competitions\nendurance runner will typically run\n45–55 miles weekly in preparation for\na race (80) which, when combined\nwith academic and social c", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["injury_safety", "training_protocol"], "text": "tes with the focus on movement quality rather than inducing high levels of fatigue.\nMST 5 movement skills training; PT 5 plyometric training; RT 5 resistance training; SC 5 speciﬁc conditioning.\nStrength and Conditioning for Adolescent Runners\nVOLUME", "language": "en", "quality_tier": "expert_review_narrative", "domain_pack": "injury_prevention_and_rehab", "review_status": "auto_classified", "needs_review": false, "prescription_permission": "explanation_only", "evidence_weight": "moderate", "auto_classification_basis": "quality_tier", "can_write_core": false}
