rence in the sub-\njects’ characteristics, as well as the definitions of\nrunning-related musculoskeletal injuries (RRMIs),\nwhich differ between studies.[5]\nStudies have been conducted to identify what are\nthe most common injuries among runners.[2,6,8,12-19]\nHowever, because of a large heterogene", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["injury_safety", "training_protocol"], "text": "syndrome, Achilles tendinopathy and plantar fasciitis were the main general\nRRMIs, while Achilles tendinopathy and patellofemoral syndrome were the\nmost common RRMIs for runners who participated in ultra-marathon races.\nRunning is one of the most po", "language": "en", "quality_tier": "peer_reviewed_study", "domain_pack": "injury_prevention_and_rehab", "review_status": "auto_classified", "needs_review": false, "prescription_permission": "explanation_only", "evidence_weight": "moderate", "auto_classification_basis": "quality_tier", "can_write_core": false}
