ic metabolic and functional\nadaptations.30 These adaptations influence performance nutri-\ntion recommendations with the overarching goals that energy\nsystems should be trained to provide the most economical\nsupport for the fuel demands of an event while other strategies\nshould ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["injury_safety"], "text": "e to the fuel\ndemands of exercise), while depletion of these stores is as-\nsociated with fatigue in the form of reduced work rates,\nimpaired skill and concentration, and increased perception\nof effort. These findings underpin the various performance", "language": "en", "quality_tier": "consensus_or_position_statement", "domain_pack": "injury_prevention_and_rehab", "review_status": "auto_classified", "needs_review": false, "prescription_permission": "can_write_core", "evidence_weight": "strong", "auto_classification_basis": "quality_tier", "can_write_core": true}
