y intake and REDs is particu-\nlarly high in female runners though comprehensive data\non exact prevalence rates remain limited [179]. Gen-\nerally, there is a lack of awareness regarding the energy\ndemands of high-intensity training [179]. REDs has far-\nreaching effects on metabolism, cardiova", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["injury_safety", "training_protocol"], "text": "of awareness regarding the energy\ndemands of high-intensity training [179]. REDs has far-\nreaching effects on metabolism, cardiovascular health,\nand reproductive function, including chronic fatigue,\nweakened immune function, menstrual irregularities", "language": "en", "quality_tier": "peer_reviewed_study", "domain_pack": "injury_prevention_and_rehab", "review_status": "auto_classified", "needs_review": false, "prescription_permission": "explanation_only", "evidence_weight": "moderate", "auto_classification_basis": "quality_tier", "can_write_core": false}
