ance. Despite\nbeing predominantly aerobic, these sports differ greatly in terms\nof energy requirements, technical execution, and competitive\nformats. Meanwhile, these disparities result in a great deal of\nvariation in intensity zone classification, training load", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["injury_safety", "training_protocol"], "text": "gement,\nwhich is crucial for striking a balance between physiological\nadaptation, performance results, and injury risk. A growing\nbody of research indicates that well-structured TID models\nstrategically modulate the training intensity, duration, and", "language": "en", "quality_tier": "peer_reviewed_study", "domain_pack": "injury_prevention_and_rehab", "review_status": "auto_classified", "needs_review": false, "prescription_permission": "explanation_only", "evidence_weight": "moderate", "auto_classification_basis": "quality_tier", "can_write_core": false}
