gy for improving\nendurance, places a strong emphasis on training inside the\ndesignated “golden intensity zone” of endurance training. Its\ntraining advantages and the physiological adaptation have garnered\ncontinuous scrutiny and have been fully corroborated for the", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["injury_safety", "training_protocol"], "text": "ing duration (Rosenblat et al., 2019). This structure lessens the\nbuildup of fatigue and facilitates sustained exercise performance\nover extended durations.\nLow-to-moderate intensity training augments aerobic metabolism\nat the physiological level by", "language": "en", "quality_tier": "peer_reviewed_study", "domain_pack": "injury_prevention_and_rehab", "review_status": "auto_classified", "needs_review": false, "prescription_permission": "explanation_only", "evidence_weight": "moderate", "auto_classification_basis": "quality_tier", "can_write_core": false}
