urther shapes model choice. During general\npreparation, PYR is advantageous for accumulating large volumes\nof low-intensity work and building aerobic capacity. In the specific\npreparation phase, coaches often introduce more Z2 and Z3 load,\nwhich may resemble a POL ", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["injury_safety", "training_protocol"], "text": "individual physiological characteristics may guide\ndistribution. Athletes with relatively low lactate thresholds may\ngain more from THR or PYR to improve performance at “golden\nintensity.” Those with high fatigue resistance or strong recovery\nability", "language": "en", "quality_tier": "peer_reviewed_study", "domain_pack": "injury_prevention_and_rehab", "review_status": "auto_classified", "needs_review": false, "prescription_permission": "explanation_only", "evidence_weight": "moderate", "auto_classification_basis": "quality_tier", "can_write_core": false}
