ion for the analyzed running sessions.\n6.2  \u0007Training Volume\nMost world-leading middle-distance runners train about\n500–600 h per year, although some 800-m runners may\ntrain for less than 400 h [25, 28, 30, 47, 54, 59]. This train-\ning volume is 40–70% of what has been reported for suc-\ncessful endurance athlete", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["injury_safety", "training_protocol"], "text": ", VO2max maximal oxygen consumption, RPE rating of perceived\nexertion, TTF time to fatigue (single effort), AWD typical accumulated work duration, Int. interval, Rec. typical recovery time (active or passive) between repetitions, prog. progressive, l", "language": "en", "quality_tier": "peer_reviewed_study", "domain_pack": "injury_prevention_and_rehab", "review_status": "auto_classified", "needs_review": false, "prescription_permission": "explanation_only", "evidence_weight": "moderate", "auto_classification_basis": "quality_tier", "can_write_core": false}
