oral pain is a common musculoskeletal-related\ncondition that is characterized by insidious onset of poorly\ndefined pain quality localized to the anterior retropatellar\nand/or peripatellar region of the knee.80 The onset of symp­\ntoms can be slow or acutely devel", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["injury_safety"], "text": "cend stairs with reduced knee flexion,\nCLINICAL PRACTICE GUIDELINES\nImpairment/Function-Based\nPREVALENCE AND INCIDENCE\nPrevalence ranges from 3% to 85% for idiopathic anterior\nknee pain (AKP) or PFP and its associated diagnoses,41,207,216\nwith a prev", "language": "en", "quality_tier": "clinical_practice_guideline", "domain_pack": "injury_prevention_and_rehab", "review_status": "auto_classified", "needs_review": false, "prescription_permission": "can_write_core", "evidence_weight": "strong", "auto_classification_basis": "quality_tier", "can_write_core": true}
