ation for each\nintervention. To maintain consistency with the most recent\ninternational expert consensus meeting on the treatment of\nPFP published in 2016,75 systematic reviews and RCTs were\nassigned levels of evidence. These levels of evidence corre­\nsponde", "keywords_zh": [], "keywords_en": [], "synonyms": [], "domain_terms": ["injury_safety"], "text": "ility impairments. Exercise therapies consist of knee-\nand/or hip-targeted exercises performed in weight-bearing\nor non–weight-bearing positions, or both. Due to the het­\nerogeneous nature and combination of multiple interven­\ntions for the treatment", "language": "en", "quality_tier": "clinical_practice_guideline", "domain_pack": "injury_prevention_and_rehab", "review_status": "auto_classified", "needs_review": false, "prescription_permission": "can_write_core", "evidence_weight": "strong", "auto_classification_basis": "quality_tier", "can_write_core": true}
